<title>UK: Charter H1 pretax profit edges up 4.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Charter H1 pretax profit edges up 4.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		38.3		   vs 35.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 9.0		    vs 8.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     51.9		   vs 49.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   570.3		  vs 585.0</p>
<p>NOTE - UK-based rail track equipment, building materials and welding products group Charter Plc said it was continuing to look for acquisition opportunities which would enhance shareholder value.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 53.5		   vs 55.2</p>
<p> Interest payable	 1.6		    vs 5.6</p>
<p> Tax charge		 15.8		   vs 16.4</p>
<p> Net taxed		  36.1		   vs 33.2</p>
<p> Retained profit	  25.4		   vs 23.1</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 8</p>
<p>Div registration date  Sept 24 (London), Sept 13 (South Africa)  Ex-div date		Sept 16</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
